  "question": {
    "text": "A conductivity cell has been calibrated with\r\n$0.01 \\mathrm{M} \\quad 1: 1$ electrolyte solution (specific conductance, $k=1.25 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{S} \\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ ) in the cell and the measured resistance was $800 \\Omega$ at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} .$ The cell constant will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LWcgV",
      "text": "$1.02 \\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hoiir",
      "text": "$0.102 \\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vh1Oa",
      "text": "$1.00 \\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "O6Be1",
      "text": "$0.5 \\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $\\mathrm{K}=1.25 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{S} \\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$\r\n$$\r\n\\rho=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{x}}=\\frac{1}{1.25 \\times 10^{-3}} \\mathrm{S}^{-1} \\mathrm{cm}\r\n$$\r\nFrom\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\nR &=\\rho \\frac{1}{A} \\\\\r\n800 &=\\frac{1}{1.25 \\times 10^{-3}} \\times \\frac{1}{A}\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$\r\n(where, $\\frac{1}{A}=$ cell constant)\r\n$\\therefore$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n\\frac{1}{A} &=800 \\times 1.25 \\times 10^{-3} \\\\\r\n&=1 \\mathrm{cm}^{-1}\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
